Ticket #4471 was marked as one parser issue, but the reports describe two causes. The export contains {reports.length} rows for {uniqueReports.length} unique report IDs, including {duplicateRows} duplicate rows. Count each ID once.

## Causes

The table describes the desk's original ticket grouping in the export. It does not reflect the follow-up GitHub issues below.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The shared parser reads dates month first even when the tenant's locale writes the day first. The `booking-v3` form has a separate problem: its `MM/DD/YYYY` hint conflicts with day-first tenants' date conventions. The hint and parser need to agree with the tenant's configured date format.

Intake tags are guesses, so the cause grouping uses tenant locale, form, and channel instead of trusting the tag.

## Follow-up

The desk separately flagged {oneDayReports} as one-day moves. They currently fall in the parser group; review their details before concluding whether all share that cause.

## Tickets

- [Parse day-first dates according to each tenant's locale](https://github.com/skacperski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
- [Align booking-v3 date hints with day-first tenant locales](https://github.com/skacperski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

